FILE: vUX-dataView.js
FEATURE: component-module
DATE: 2026-09-17
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'component-teardown'

REASON
DataView now delegates to src/componentEngine.js instead of carrying its own
buildRow()/reconcile()/cells machinery.

The public surface is unchanged: initialize, setData, updateRow, sort, filter,
getData, destroy, config.key and config.data all behave exactly as before, and
every error message is preserved verbatim - including 'the row object at index N'
and 'a string naming the unique key field of each row object', which is why the
engine takes an itemNoun and why config.key keeps its own validateString call
rather than using the engine's generic helper.

What consumers gain: a row template now accepts the engine's whole binding set,
not just data-v-field. data-v-bind, data-v-on, data-v-ref, data-v-show and
data-v-class work in rows, and config.handlers and config.formatters were added to
support them.

Two behaviour notes:

  - updateRow() now merges into the row and writes the merged object back into the
    model. Previously it mutated the row object in place, which meant getData()
    handed back objects the view was still using. Externally the observable result
    is the same, except that getData() is now safe to hold on to.

  - destroy() now clears 'initialized'. It did not before, which made the
    'This DataView has been destroyed' guard in initialize() unreachable: a
    re-initialize after destroy silently did nothing instead of reporting itself.
    The message was already written; it now actually fires.


